myelin 1
id      openai
about   OpenAI Node SDK 7 (openai@7.43): bans v3-era Configuration/OpenAIApi, removed helpers and namespaces, and the deprecated Assistants, Chat Completions functions/max_tokens, and Realtime beta and Sora surfaces
fires   openai | openai-node | openai sdk | chat.completions | responses.create | new OpenAI
comments skip
status  Researched 2026-10-26 against openai 7.43.0 (npm latest). Rules come from the package's own @deprecated tags and CHANGELOG, plus openai-node README/MIGRATION and discussion #217. Snippets and good bench files type-checked (tsc --strict) against openai@7.43.0 and zod 4.6.7; not executed against the API. platform.openai.com deprecations page unreachable from the build sandbox, so model-retirement rules are omitted.

= version     openai 7.43.0 (npm latest, published 2026-10-22)
= verified    2026-10-26
= node.min    22 (package engines >=22; Node 20 is end of life per the README)
= client      import OpenAI from "openai"; new OpenAI() reads OPENAI_API_KEY from the environment
= primary     client.responses.create / .stream / .parse; read response.output_text. Chat Completions (client.chat.completions) is still supported.
= tools       Chat: tools: [{ type: "function", function: {...} }] + tool_choice. Responses: flat { type: "function", name, parameters }.
= tokens      Chat: max_completion_tokens. Responses: max_output_tokens.
= structured  zodResponseFormat from "openai/helpers/zod" with client.chat.completions.parse, or client.responses.parse
= runner      client.chat.completions.runTools({ model, messages, tools }) with functionToolCall / finalFunctionToolCall events

! O1 /\bOpenAIApi\b|\bnew\s+Configuration\s*\(\s*\{\s*apiKey\b/   The v3 client (Configuration + OpenAIApi) is gone. Use import OpenAI from "openai" and new OpenAI({ apiKey }). -> $init
! O2 /\.(?:createChatCompletion|createCompletion)\s*\(/          openai.createChatCompletion / createCompletion are v3 methods. Use client.chat.completions.create or client.responses.create. -> $responses
! O3 /\.data\.choices\b/                                          v4+ responses are not wrapped in .data. Read completion.choices[0].message directly. -> $responses
! O4 /\bbeta\.(?:assistants|threads)\b/                          The Assistants API (client.beta.assistants, beta.threads) is deprecated in favour of the Responses API. Use client.responses.create and carry state with previous_response_id. -> $responses
! O5 /\bbeta\.chat\b/                                            beta.chat was removed. Call client.chat.completions.parse(), .stream() or .runTools() on the main namespace. -> $parse
! O6 /\bbeta\.realtime\b/                                        The old beta Realtime API is deprecated; Realtime is generally available. Use client.realtime.
! O7 /\bfunction_call\s*:/                                       function_call is deprecated in favour of tool_choice (Chat Completions). Send tools and tool_choice. -> $tools
! O8 /\bfunctions\s*:\s*\[/                                      functions[] is deprecated in favour of tools[]. Each entry becomes { type: "function", function: { name, parameters } }. -> $tools
! O9 /\brole\s*:\s*['"]function['"]/                             The function message role is deprecated. Answer a tool call with { role: "tool", tool_call_id, content }. -> $tools
! O10 /\bmax_tokens\s*:/ unless /@anthropic-ai|\bAnthropic\b|\bclaude-/i   max_tokens is deprecated on Chat Completions and rejected by reasoning models. Use max_completion_tokens (Responses: max_output_tokens). -> $tokens
! O11 /\brunFunctions\s*\(/                                      runFunctions was removed in openai v5. Use client.chat.completions.runTools({ model, messages, tools }). -> $runner
! O12 /\bOpenAI\.fileFromPath\b/                                 OpenAI.fileFromPath was removed. Pass fs.createReadStream(path) to files.create.
! O13 /\.(?:completions|files|models|responses|vectorStores|assistants|threads|messages|evals|containers)\.del\s*\(/   The HTTP del methods were renamed to delete, e.g. client.files.delete(id).
! O14 /\b(?:openai|client)\.videos\.(?:create|retrieve|list|delete|remix|downloadContent|edit|extend)\s*\(/   The Sora video API (client.videos) was scheduled to shut down on 2026-09-24 (SDK @deprecated tags). Do not write new video code against it.
! O15 /\bnew\s+OpenAI\s*\(\s*\{[^}]*\bhttpAgent\s*:/             httpAgent was removed from the client. Pass fetchOptions instead, e.g. fetchOptions: { dispatcher } with undici's ProxyAgent.
! O16 /\.on\(\s*['"](?:functionCall|functionCallResult|finalFunctionCall|finalFunctionCallResult)['"]|\.(?:finalFunctionCall|finalFunctionCallResult)\s*\(/   runTools events and methods were renamed: functionToolCall, functionToolCallResult, finalFunctionToolCall, finalFunctionToolCallResult. -> $runner

~ P1 Use client.responses.create for new code; read response.output_text. Chat Completions keeps working.
~ P2 Structured output: client.chat.completions.parse with zodResponseFormat from "openai/helpers/zod", and read choices[0].message.parsed.
~ P3 Let the SDK run the tool loop with runTools instead of hand-writing the call-and-reply cycle.
~ P4 Pass the key through the environment (OPENAI_API_KEY) and omit apiKey; the constructor reads it.
~ P5 Chat Completions stays supported indefinitely; do not rewrite working Chat code only to change APIs.

$ init
import OpenAI from "openai";

const client = new OpenAI(); // reads OPENAI_API_KEY from the environment
$$

$ responses
import OpenAI from "openai";

const client = new OpenAI();

const response = await client.responses.create({
  model: "gpt-5.5",
  instructions: "You are a concise assistant.",
  input: "Summarise the plot of Hamlet in two sentences.",
});

console.log(response.output_text);
$$

$ tools
import OpenAI from "openai";

const client = new OpenAI();

const completion = await client.chat.completions.create({
  model: "gpt-5.5",
  messages: [{ role: "user", content: "What is the weather in Oslo?" }],
  tools: [
    {
      type: "function",
      function: {
        name: "get_weather",
        description: "Get the current weather for a city",
        parameters: {
          type: "object",
          properties: { city: { type: "string" } },
          required: ["city"],
          additionalProperties: false,
        },
        strict: true,
      },
    },
  ],
  tool_choice: "auto",
});

const message = completion.choices[0].message;
for (const call of message.tool_calls ?? []) {
  console.log(call.type === "function" ? call.function.name : call.type);
}
$$

$ tokens
import OpenAI from "openai";

const client = new OpenAI();
const messages = [{ role: "user" as const, content: "Give me three fun facts about octopuses." }];

const completion = await client.chat.completions.create({
  model: "gpt-5.5",
  messages,
  max_completion_tokens: 512,
});

console.log(completion.choices[0].message.content);
$$

$ parse
import OpenAI from "openai";
import { zodResponseFormat } from "openai/helpers/zod";
import { z } from "zod";

const client = new OpenAI();

const CalendarEvent = z.object({
  name: z.string(),
  date: z.string(),
  participants: z.array(z.string()),
});

const completion = await client.chat.completions.parse({
  model: "gpt-5.5",
  messages: [{ role: "user", content: "Alice and Bob meet on Friday for a demo." }],
  response_format: zodResponseFormat(CalendarEvent, "event"),
});

console.log(completion.choices[0].message.parsed);
$$

$ runner
import OpenAI from "openai";

const client = new OpenAI();

const runner = client.chat.completions.runTools({
  model: "gpt-5.5",
  messages: [{ role: "user", content: "What is the weather in Oslo?" }],
  tools: [
    {
      type: "function",
      function: {
        name: "get_weather",
        description: "Get the current weather for a city",
        parameters: {
          type: "object",
          properties: { city: { type: "string" } },
          required: ["city"],
        },
        function: (args: string) => `Sunny in ${JSON.parse(args).city}`,
      },
    },
  ],
});

runner.on("functionToolCallResult", (content) => console.log("tool result:", content));
console.log(await runner.finalContent());
$$
